<project name="U7L2p4-Mondrian" app="Snap! 12.0.6, https://snap.berkeley.edu" version="2"><notes></notes><thumbnail>data:image/png;base64,</thumbnail><scenes select="1"><scene name="U7L2p4-Mondrian"><notes></notes><hidden></hidden><headers></headers><code></code><blocks><block-definition s="Mondrian, level: %&apos;level&apos; width: %&apos;width&apos; height: %&apos;height&apos;" type="command" category="looks"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%n"></input><input type="%n"></input><input type="%n"></input></inputs><script><block s="doIfElse"><block s="reportVariadicEquals"><list><block var="level"/><l>1</l></list></block><script><custom-block s="rectangle, width: %n height: %n"><block var="width"/><block var="height"/><comment w="53.333333333333336" collapsed="true">7.2.4.5</comment></custom-block></script><script><block s="doDeclareVariables"><list><l>fraction</l></list></block><block s="doSetVar"><l>fraction</l><block s="reportRandom"><l>0.2</l><l>0.8</l></block></block><block s="doIfElse"><block s="reportNot"><block s="reportVariadicGreaterThan"><list><block var="width"/><block var="height"/></list></block></block><script><custom-block s="Mondrian, level: %n width: %n height: %n"><block s="reportDifference"><block var="level"/><l>1</l></block><block var="width"/><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block var="fraction"/><block var="height"/></list></block></custom-block><block s="forward"><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block var="fraction"/><block var="height"/></list></block></block><custom-block s="Mondrian, level: %n width: %n height: %n"><block s="reportDifference"><block var="level"/><l>1</l></block><block var="width"/><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block s="reportDifference"><l>1</l><block var="fraction"/></block><block var="height"/></list></block></custom-block><block s="forward"><block s="reportDifference"><l>0</l><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block var="fraction"/><block var="height"/></list></block></block><comment w="114.66666666666667" collapsed="true">State transparency</comment></block></script><script><block s="forward"><block var="height"/></block><block s="turn"><l>90</l></block><custom-block s="Mondrian, level: %n width: %n height: %n"><block var="level"/><block var="height"/><block var="width"/><comment w="68" collapsed="true">See below.</comment></custom-block><block s="turnLeft"><l>90</l></block><block s="forward"><block s="reportDifference"><l>0</l><block var="height"/></block></block></script><comment w="53.333333333333336" collapsed="true">7.2.4.6</comment></block></script></block></script><scripts><comment x="11.666666666666666" y="510.7999999999999" w="371.3333333333333" collapsed="false">The last recursive call above elegantly interchanges width and height, at the same level, so that height will be greater than width and the code in the other branch of the IF will be run.  Note that the Boolean expression has to include the case in which the two dimensions are equal; otherwise, the recursive call will take the second branch again, and an infinite loop results.&#xD;&#xD;If that all seems too heady, that recursive call can be replaced with the four commands below, which duplicate the pattern of the first branch of the IF.  The move and turn to get the sprite in position, and the turn and move to undo them, are still required. </comment><script x="13.666666666666668" y="674.1111111111114"><custom-block s="Mondrian, level: %n width: %n height: %n"><block s="reportDifference"><block var="level"/><l>1</l></block><block var="height"/><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block var="fraction"/><block var="width"/></list></block></custom-block><block s="forward"><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block var="fraction"/><block var="width"/></list></block></block><custom-block s="Mondrian, level: %n width: %n height: %n"><block s="reportDifference"><block var="level"/><l>1</l></block><block var="height"/><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block s="reportDifference"><l>1</l><block var="fraction"/></block><block var="width"/></list></block></custom-block><block s="forward"><block s="reportDifference"><l>0</l><block s="reportVariadicProduct"><list><block var="fraction"/><block var="width"/></list></block></block></block></script></scripts></block-definition><block-definition s="rectangle, width: %&apos;width&apos; height: %&apos;height&apos;" type="command" category="looks"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%n"></input><input type="%n"></input></inputs><script><custom-block s="set pen to black line"></custom-block><block s="down"></block><block s="doRepeat"><l>2</l><script><block s="forward"><block var="height"/></block><block s="turn"><l>90</l></block><block s="forward"><block var="width"/></block><block s="turn"><l>90</l></block></script></block><block s="up"><comment w="127.33333333333333" collapsed="true">End of common code.</comment></block><block s="forward"><block s="reportQuotient"><block var="height"/><l>2</l></block><comment w="72.66666666666667" collapsed="true">version 1</comment></block><block s="turn"><l>90</l></block><custom-block s="set pen to paint with thickness: %n"><block var="height"/></custom-block><block s="down"></block><block s="forward"><block var="width"/></block><block s="up"></block><block s="forward"><block s="reportDifference"><l>0</l><block var="width"/></block></block><block s="turnLeft"><l>90</l></block><block s="forward"><block s="reportQuotient"><block var="height"/><l>-2</l></block></block></script><scripts><script x="15.333333333333336" y="458.6666666666667"><block s="changeXPosition"><l>5</l><comment w="80.66666666666667" collapsed="true">version 2</comment></block><block s="changeYPosition"><l>5</l></block><block s="doRun"><block s="reportListItem"><l><option>random</option></l><block var="colors"/></block><list></list></block><block s="floodFill"></block><block s="changeXPosition"><l>-5</l></block><block s="changeYPosition"><l>-5</l></block></script><comment x="202.66666666666669" y="69.46666666666667" w="329.3333333333333" collapsed="false">Here are two approaches to drawing the rectangle.&#xD;The code from the beginning to the PEN UP draws the outer black border. The difference is in how to fill the inside of the rectangle.  Version 1 uses the idea given in the lab, drawing a very thick line in color.  Version 2 may be easier to understand; it uses the FILL block instead.  To use FILL we have to pick the pen up and then move inside the rectangle, but that may be conceptually easier to undo than moving halfway up and then all the way across, in version 1.</comment></scripts></block-definition><block-definition s="paint color: %&apos;color&apos; shade: %&apos;shade&apos;" type="reporter" category="pen"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%s"></input><input type="%s"></input></inputs><script><block s="doReport"><block s="reportNewList"><list><block var="color"/><block var="shade"/></list></block></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="set pen to black line" type="command" category="pen"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs></inputs><script><block s="setSize"><l>5</l></block><block s="setPenColorDimension"><l><option>brightness</option></l><l>0</l></block><block s="doSetGlobalFlag"><l><option>flat line ends</option></l><l><bool>false</bool></l></block></script></block-definition><block-definition s="set pen to paint with thickness: %&apos;thickness&apos;" type="command" category="pen"><header></header><code></code><translations></translations><inputs><input type="%n"></input></inputs><script><block s="setSize"><block var="thickness"/></block><block s="doRun"><block s="reportListItem"><l><option>random</option></l><block var="colors"/></block><list></list></block><block s="doSetGlobalFlag"><l><option>flat line ends</option></l><l><bool>true</bool></l></block></script></bloc